menu "Lyra JC3248W535EN display"

choice LYRA_DISPLAY_PIPELINE
    prompt "Display pipeline"
    default LYRA_DISPLAY_STREAMED_BANDS
    help
        Selects how LVGL output reaches the AXS15231B panel.

    config LYRA_DISPLAY_STREAMED_BANDS
        bool "Streamed bands in internal RAM"
        help
            LVGL renders horizontal bands into two internal DMA buffers. Each
            band is sent to the panel while the next one is rendered, so
            drawing and the QSPI transfer overlap and no PSRAM framebuffer
            traffic competes with audio. Redraws start at row zero, as the
            panel requires.

    config LYRA_DISPLAY_LEGACY_FRAMEBUFFER
        bool "Legacy PSRAM framebuffer"
        help
            The previous pipeline: LVGL draws into one PSRAM framebuffer and a
            display task copies rows into small DMA strips after each frame.
            Rendering and transfer run one after the other. Keep only for
            comparison or as a fallback during board bring-up.
endchoice

config LYRA_DISPLAY_BAND_LINES
    int "Rows per streamed band"
    depends on LYRA_DISPLAY_STREAMED_BANDS
    range 8 48
    default 24
    help
        Height of each of the two internal DMA render buffers. Each row costs
        640 bytes per buffer, so 24 rows use 30 KiB of internal RAM in total.
        Taller bands reduce per-band LVGL overhead; shorter bands leave more
        internal RAM for audio and Wi-Fi. If the buffers cannot be allocated
        at boot, the firmware halves the height until they fit.

choice LYRA_LCD_QSPI_CLOCK
    prompt "LCD QSPI pixel clock"
    default LYRA_LCD_QSPI_CLOCK_40MHZ
    help
        The ESP32-S3 SPI clock is derived from the 80 MHz APB clock, so only
        integer divisors are available. Earlier firmware requested 50 MHz,
        which the driver rounds down to 40 MHz.

    config LYRA_LCD_QSPI_CLOCK_40MHZ
        bool "40 MHz"

    config LYRA_LCD_QSPI_CLOCK_80MHZ
        bool "80 MHz (experimental)"
        help
            Halves panel transfer time. The panel signals are routed through
            the GPIO matrix and the AXS15231B rating at this clock is not
            documented for this board. Validate for corrupted or shifted rows
            on the physical kit before keeping this setting.
endchoice

config LYRA_LCD_QSPI_CLOCK_MHZ
    int
    default 80 if LYRA_LCD_QSPI_CLOCK_80MHZ
    default 40

endmenu
